  "title": "Government restricts 2-compound fixed drug combinations for children under 4",
  "summary": "The Indian government has imposed stricter restrictions on fixed dose combinations containing Chlorpheniramine Maleate and Phenylephrine Hydrochloride, mandating warnings to children under four. This is a significant step to ensure the safety and health of young children, following expert recommendations and a recent decision by the Drugs Technical Advisory Board.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The government implemented restrictions on all formulations containing Chlorpheniramine Maleate and Phenylephrine Hydrochloride.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The decision was based on recommendations from an expert committee and the Drugs Technical Advisory Board (DTAB).",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The latest notification extends the requirement to all formulations containing these two ingredients.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
